Title: Judge's X Word Puzzle No. 17
Author: J. Flanagan
Date: 1927-08-20
Byline: Submitted by J. Flanagan, Columbus, O. Judge pays $10 for each puzzle printed.
Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-08-20_93/page/n27/mode/1up
Puzzle-Number: 17
Solution-Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-08-27_93/page/n31/mode/1up


CHOPSTICKS#KISS
R#HE.RT#E#TIN#T
IS#ANY#TRAIN#MA
TOP#E#RANGE#SOR
ILLS#MELEE#RIDE
COY#LEVEL#OOZES
AS#TIRES#HIVES#
L#FRAIL#HOLES#D
#BLURT#LOVER#PI
GL.SS#TATER#HOP
HOST#YODEL#GIRL
OAK#CAMEL#J#DUO
ST#WOMAN#FAG#SM
T#PEP#T#MOVER#A
SCAT#POLYGAMIST


A1. What do they use in China to get dinner? ~ CHOPSTICKS
A8. Name something two and two can make. ~ KISS
A11. What is lost and won in the Love game? ~ HE.RT
A12. What can be found in a Ford in the moonlight? ~ TIN
A13. Name another word for exists. ~ IS
A15. Name an indefinite pronoun. ~ ANY
A16. What leaves tracks behind—after it goes by? ~ TRAIN
A18. Who is the speaker of the house? ~ MA
A19. What goes around a lot? ~ TOP
A21. What are big guns often found on? ~ RANGE
A22. What is an Irishman's title of respect? ~ SOR
A23. What brings the doctor's bills? ~ ILLS
A24. What is a free-for-all in Ireland? ~ MELEE
A25. What does Sande do? ~ RIDE
A26. What are flappers everything else but? ~ COY
A27. What instrument is used to tell when a thing is on the level? ~ LEVEL
A28. How does water leave the spring? ~ OOZES
A29. What little adverb expresses equality? ~ AS
A30. What are much better after they get the air? ~ TIRES
A31. What are apt to break out—even at Sing Sing? ~ HIVES
A32. What adjective means fragile; weak? ~ FRAIL
A33. What is the aim of all golfers? (plural). ~ HOLES
A35. Give a word meaning "to speak inadvertently." ~ BLURT
A36. Who is the florist's best customer? ~ LOVER
A37. What is printshop pastry? ~ PI
A38. Name something easily seen through. ~ GL.SS
A39. What is a potato to a Southern darky? ~ TATER
A40. Give another word for spring. ~ HOP
A41. Name an entertaining person. ~ HOST
A42. What should you do when you miss your Swiss? ~ YODEL
A43. What takes up about 99 99-100 per cent of a college boy's thoughts? ~ GIRL
A44. Name a tree, the bark of which is used for tanning. ~ OAK
A45. What can get along for days without a drink? ~ CAMEL
A47. What double crime is often perpetrated in vaudeville houses? ~ DUO
A48. Name something very dangerous to cross (abbr.). ~ ST
A49. What came after man—and is still after him? ~ WOMAN
A50. What was the big smoke to Tommy—over there? ~ FAG
A52. What is an abbreviation for Soused Mackerals? ~ SM
A53. What does Mr. Babbit do business with? ~ PEP
A54. What is indispensable to moving day? ~ MOVER
A56. What should be told to every noisy old cat? ~ SCAT
A57. Name a heavy investor in the love business. ~ POLYGAMIST

D1. What is George Jean Nathan? ~ CRITICAL
D2. Name an exclamation of surprise. ~ OH
D3. What is usually lost in a shell game? ~ PEA
D4. What must you be—or go crazy? ~ S.NE
D5. What must you do to attain success? ~ TRY
D6. What does Elinor Glyn write about? ~ IT
D7. What does every nut have? ~ KERNEL
D8. What are domestic relations? ~ KIN
D9. Name a preposition of place. ~ IN
D10. What follows the girls around? ~ STARES
D12. What is always hanging around a sheik's neck? ~ TIE
D14. What crimes are committed singly? ~ SOLOS
D16. What do all "cats" carry? ~ TALES
D17. What is old stuff? ~ AGE
D18. Name something always stylish. ~ MODES
D20. What verb means to employ with diligence? ~ PLY
D21. Name a very noisy affair. ~ REVEL
D22. What do shoes come in? ~ SIZES
D24. What helped Lindbergh get across? ~ MERIT
D25. What kind of person is rarely ever found at home? ~ ROVER
D27. What kind of people are often admitted to the bar? ~ LIARS
D28. Name a person who makes things run smoothly. ~ OILER
D30. What would you like to place in your bank? ~ TRUST
D31. Name a poor kind of place to live in. ~ HOVEL
D32. What holds its liquor well? ~ FL.SK
D33. Where does a 60c meal usually cost $2.50? ~ HOTEL
D34. What is a man who remembers a woman's birthday but forgets her age? ~ DIPLOMAT
D35. What is a swell verb? ~ BLOAT
D36. What word means to be well-loaded? ~ LADEN
D37. What King of India fought against Alexander? ~ PORUS
D38. What spirits are never popular? ~ GHOSTS
D39. What strikes a ham actor—and runs? ~ TOMATO
D40. What are speak-easies to the eye of the law? ~ HID
D42. What is the sweet potato of the South Seas? ~ YAM
D45. Name an arresting personality. ~ COP
D46. Name a Dutch possession in Malaysea. ~ JAVA
D49. What is the U. S. A. since Prohibition? ~ WET
D50. What does a Londoner walk through from Chelsea to the Strand? ~ FOG
D51. What is precious to most women? ~ GEM
D53. Who is it that pays and pays? ~ PA
D54. Name a possessive pronoun. ~ MY
D55. In what state is Pawtucket? (init.) ~ RI


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A52: What is an abbreviation for Soused Mackerals? → Mackerels
D46: Name a Dutch possession in Malaysea. → Malaysia

